  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 205 AM EDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\n- Periods of Rain and Thunderstorms Tonight into Next Week\n\nDry conditions are expected today with areas to the southeast\nstaying dry into Wednesday afternoon. Our next chance for rain\nmoves in late tonight with a slow moving front. Instability will\nbe limited with the front around 500 J/kg as seen in the HREF and\nother ensembles. Paired with shear around 20 to 30 knots, not\nexpecting any severe weather into Wednesday. However with the slow\nmoving boundary, synoptic support with the upper level jet\ndivergence and positive vorticity advection, along with \nprecipitable water values increasing to 1.5 to 2 inches there will\nbe a potential for localized spots of 1-3 inches of rain. Areas \nthat see showers and storms repeatedly train over have the best \nchance of seeing these higher end amounts. The front will slowly \nshift east of the area Thursday with dry conditions returning \nThursday night.\n\nOverall in the upper level flow we'll remain under a broad trough.\nWithin this regime, multiple shortwaves are expected to track\nthrough the region bringing additional chances for showers and\nthunderstorms. Long range ensembles are in decent agreement with \nmost if not all members showing rainfall accumulations over the \nweekend into next week. Most members highlight 24 hour amounts \nunder an inch, there are a small number of members that show \nhigher amounts up to 2 inches. Not any one day looks to be a \ncomplete washout with periods of dry time.",
